// URL policy (plan P3-20; design T9 A2): which references a document may
// make, by use — one table for the engine (safeImageSrc, safeLinkUrl:
// engine/src/support/url_policy.gen.h) and the host's locator (urlAllowed:
// runtime/src/shared/url_policy.gen.mjs), generated by tools/gen-schema.mjs.
//
// A relative reference (no scheme: a path, a query, a fragment) is allowed
// for every use. A scheme is whatever precedes the first ':' that comes
// before any '/', '?' or '#', compared exactly, lowercased — a scheme
// spelled with tabs or spaces is no allowed one.
//
// SCHEME(name, uses, prefix)
//   uses:   image (an image's src), link (a link's or a reference's href),
//           load (an execute-time load: $.load, #bibliography)
//   prefix: what the rest after "name:" must start with ("" = anything)
SCHEME(http, image link load, "")
SCHEME(https, image link load, "")
SCHEME(mailto, link, "")
SCHEME(data, image, "image/")
